<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - Codan Bank sees higher Danish 1997 GDP.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Codan Bank sees higher Danish 1997 GDP.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey Denmark's Codan Bank on Wednesday raised its expectations for Denmark's 1997 GDP (gross domestic product) growth to 2.8 percent from 2.5 percent in its last forecast in October last year.</p>
<p>At the same time it upped its 1997 forecast for the current account surplus to 13.5 billion crowns from 10.0 billion crowns, cutting its estimate for inflation to 2.25 percent from 2.5 percent.</p>
<p>The latest Danish Economy Ministry forecast in December foresaw 2.9 percent GDP growth, 2.3 percent inflation, 8.0 percent unemployment and a current account surplus of 13.0 billion crowns for this year.</p>
<p>The following estimates were made by 10 leading local and international organisations.</p>
<p>	  (pct)	 GDP    inflation  unemployment c/a (bln Dkk)</p>
<p>Codan Bank (1/97)   2.8    2.25	 7.7	   13.5</p>
<p>Danske Bank(12/96)  2.75   2.25	 8.0	   14.1</p>
<p>Citibank (12/96)    2.9    2.4	  8.2	   15.0</p>
<p>Paribas (12/96)     2.7    2.7	   --	    --</p>
<p>PaineWebber (12/96) 2.3    2.5	  7.5	   10.2</p>
<p>Morgan St   (12/96) 3.1    2.6	  8.6	   13.0</p>
<p>Lehman Bros (12/96) 2.6    2.4	  8.5	    --</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs(11/96)3.6    2.6	  8.4	    9.5</p>
<p>Conf Dan Ind (11/96)2.5    2.3	  --	    12.0</p>
<p>NatWest(11/96)	2.9    2.6	  8.8	    8.3</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
